You already opened up the can of worms when you woke Rodney,
actually.

Speaking from personal experience, there are a lot of situations where
the ability to jump can avoid combat.  However, you don't necessarily
need the boots.  If you have the ability to cast a judicious jump or
two on Astral it'll be a big help.  The situation that can easily come
up is when one kills a Rider inside a door while on the door square
but then an angel steps onto that square.  At that point you can't zap
teleport because that will revive the Rider.  However, zapping
teleport diagonally and then jumping works fine.  So, either one has
to be more judicious in where they let the Riders fall or elsewand of
striking the door or something.  The other issue is that the Riders
move surprisingly fast and a jump escapes from melee with them while
walking sometimes won't.
>
> The short of it seems to be that in no teleport levels (for the PC) that
